course: dictionary
lesson: 1437
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a thing, a layer of something, or an action. Carpet is a noun when it names the thick cloth on a floor: «mud on the carpet» means mud on that cloth.
explain: Look at the words around carpet to find its job. «A carpet of leaves» means a thick layer of leaves on the ground, because the word of tells you the carpet is a layer of something. Phrases change the meaning too: a red carpet is a special welcome.
explain: Carpet can also be a verb. To carpet a room means to cover its floor with carpet. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A carpet is a thick cloth that covers a floor.
fact: Carpet can also mean a thick layer on the ground, as in «a carpet of leaves».
fact: As a verb, to carpet a room means to cover its floor with carpet.
fact: «Red carpet» means a special welcome, and «sweep under the carpet» means to hide a problem.
fact: Soft materials such as curtains and carpets absorb sound and reduce echoes.
exercise: «At home it happens all the time: mud on the carpet, an empty biscuit tin.» What is the carpet here? | To hide a problem | *A thick cloth that covers the floor | A thick layer of leaves on the ground | A special welcome
exercise: «A carpet of leaves covered the path.» What does carpet mean here? | A special welcome | To cover a floor with cloth | *A thick layer on the ground | To hide a problem
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Let's carpet the new room this weekend.» What does carpet mean here? | To wash the clothes | To make a loud noise | To sweep up the dust | *To cover the floor with carpet
test: «They rolled out the red carpet for the visiting team.» What does red carpet mean? | To hide a problem | A red floor covering | A thick layer of leaves | *A special welcome
test: «Try not to sweep the problem under the carpet.» What does this phrase mean? | To carpet a room | *To hide a problem | To sweep up the dust | To clean the carpet fast
exam: Which sentence uses carpet as a verb? | «A carpet of leaves covered the path» | «Soft curtains and carpets absorb sound» | «Mud on the carpet made the kitchen messy» | *«We will carpet the hall next week»
